ve to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Park Hotels & Resorts Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.2B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $102M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -8.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 10.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 16017% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":160.16906339522407},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 519% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.8pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 24% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 39% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Park Hotels & Resorts Inc (PK) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: RevPAR Jumps 8. ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/park-hotels-resorts-inc-pk-011911625.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793927951.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Park Hotels & Resorts (PK) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/park-hotels-resorts-pk-q3-223258000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793918967.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Park Hotels & Resorts declares $0.25 dividend (NYSE:PK)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666919-park-hotels-and-resorts-declares-0_25-dividend","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793898134.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Park Hotels & Resorts (NYSE:PK) Announces Quarterly Earnings Result